Scope note

This licence covers the source code, documentation and configuration authored in
this repository. It does not and cannot relicense third-party material:

* The NIST Chemistry WebBook reference extract described under data/reference/ is NOT
  distributed with this repository, and is not in its history. NIST Standard Reference
  Data is a statutory exception to the public-domain status of US Government works
  (Standard Reference Data Act, Public Law 90-396), the WebBook asserts copyright, and
  nothing retrieved from NIST establishes that citation alone permits redistributing an
  extract. This project therefore takes the non-redistribution route. That is a
  conservative publication decision, not an adjudication of copyright exceptions.
  data/reference/ keeps only metadata -- request URLs, units, row counts, per-property
  citations and SHA-256 digests -- which reproduces no retrieved value. Obtain the
  values yourself under your own access basis; see data/reference/README.md and
  docs/release/PUBLIC_DATA_POLICY.md.
* No third-party dataset, simulator deck, book, paper or binary is distributed here.
  Where a study uses one, the repository stores retrieval instructions and checksums,
  and the third party's own licence governs the material itself.
